{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":26473,"name":"Telmo","username":"T_Silva","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/t_silva/{size}/11946_2.png","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:13:21.281Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCKB Pulse: who is building on CKB, live\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHi everyone,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe made CKB Pulse, a page that shows the public work on CKB as it happens on GitHub.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://pulse-lab.lusocryptolabs.com\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n      \u003cimg class=\"site-icon\" alt=\"\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://pulse-lab.lusocryptolabs.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCKB Pulse\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"aspect-image\" style=\"--aspect-ratio:690/361;\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/0/0b115ace4434d4ac7dbb74ee46142db794f3b11f_2_690x362.png\" class=\"thumbnail\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"272E19\" width=\"690\" height=\"362\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://pulse-lab.lusocryptolabs.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eCKB Pulse · Last 7 days\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003e627 updates by 62 people in 58 projects, in the last 7 days.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eEvery project is a block. When someone pushes code, proposes or reviews a change, reports a problem or publishes a release, a light flies from their face to the project and the block grows. Watch it live, or replay the last 24 hours or the last 7 days in a minute or two. Drag to turn the view, tap a block to open the project.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt is written for people who never open GitHub too: plain words, in English, 中文 and Português.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat you can see\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHighlights of the day, the week and the month: the most active projects, people and organisations, with medals.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eActive developers per month over the last two years, and how many committed for the first time.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNew CKB projects from the last 14 days, flagged when they appear. Follow projects and people on your device and get a notice when they move.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFor projects with contracts on mainnet: the CKB in cells that use them, transactions and last use, from the CKB explorer and the ckb-cli deployment files the project commits.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA picture to share for the highlights, any project or any person.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe counters at the top open everything as plain lists, for keyboards and screen readers.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHow it finds projects\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNobody keeps the list by hand. Every few hours it searches GitHub for repositories that use CKB libraries (CCC, Lumos, Spore, RGB++, JoyID, ckb-std, the Go and Java SDKs and more) or carry CKB topics. It also checks the other projects of the people working in them, and the repositories behind scripts registered on the CKB explorer. A new organisation appears on its own when it starts working, and leaves after 30 days without work by people.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMissing a project? Add a topic such as \u003ccode\u003eckb\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003enervos\u003c/code\u003e to its repository, or type the GitHub name in the “New” tab, under “Missing someone?”. It joins when GitHub shows public CKB work from the last 30 days.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHow it counts\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnly work by people. Bots, AI agents working on their own branches (\u003ccode\u003eclaude/\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003ecodex/\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003ecopilot/\u003c/code\u003e and others) and the same update pushed day after day by a script show as grey sparks and stay out of the numbers and medals. Merging an agent’s work still counts. For medals, one person counts at most 10 updates per project per hour.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGitHub’s public events arrive 30 seconds to a few hours late, so live means as soon as GitHub tells us.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe code is open, MIT: \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/LusoCryptoLabs/ckb-pulse\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eGitHub - LusoCryptoLabs/ckb-pulse: Live GitHub activity of the CKB ecosystem, drawn in 3D · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat would you like to see on it, and who is missing?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-10-10T02:13:21.281Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":7,"reads":28,"readers_count":27,"score":199.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":10862,"topic_slug":"ckb-pulse-who-is-building-on-ckb-live","display_username":"Telmo","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://pulse-lab.lusocryptolabs.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"CKB Pulse","clicks":9},{"url":"https://github.com/LusoCryptoLabs/ckb-pulse","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - LusoCryptoLabs/ckb-pulse: Live GitHub activity of the CKB ecosystem, drawn in 3D · GitHub","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":9}],"